hadiths[12]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21051","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: do you see this old man, meaning himself? I spoke to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate with him, and I saw the mark between his shoulders, and it is at the edge of the cartilage of his left shoulder, like a gathered fist, meaning the gathered palm, and he said with his hand and closed it, upon it moles like warts."
"21052","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out traveling, would say: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, and the sadness of return, and decrease after increase, and the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight regarding family and wealth."
"21053","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Asim informed us, at Kufa, and I did not write it, then I heard Shubah narrating it and I recognized it by it, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled, said: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, and the sadness of return, and decrease after increase, and the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight regarding family and wealth."
"21054","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled, said: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, and the sadness of return, and decrease after increase, and the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight regarding family and wealth."
"21055","Abu Said narrated to us, Thabit narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, that he saw the seal between the shoulders of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but he had no companionship."
"21056","Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: let none of you urinate in a hole. And when you sleep, extinguish the lamp, for the mouse takes the wick and burns the people of the house. And tie the waterskins, and cover the drink, and close the doors at night. They said to Qatadah: what is disliked about urinating in a hole? He said: it is said they are dwellings of the jinn."
"21057","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, Asim said: and he had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out on a journey, said: O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, and the sadness of return, and decrease after increase, and the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight regarding wealth and family. And when he returned, he said similar to it, except that he says: and an evil sight regarding family and wealth, beginning with family."
"21058","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: the prayer was established, the dawn prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying the two rakahs of Fajr, and he said to him: with which of your two prayers did you reckon? With your prayer alone, or your prayer which you prayed with us?"
"21059","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ate with him from his food, and I said: may Allah forgive you, O Messenger of Allah. Then I said: did he ask forgiveness for you? Shubah said: or a man said to him. He said: yes, and for you. And he recited: and ask forgiveness for your sin and for the believing men and believing women. Then I looked at the cartilage of his right shoulder, or his left shoulder, Shubah is the one who doubts, and it was like a gathered fist with warts upon it."
"21060","Bakr ibn Isa Abu Bishr al-Rasibi narrated to us, Thabit Abu Zayd al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, that he said: Abdullah ibn Sarjis had seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that he had no companionship."
"21061","Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, they said: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I entered upon him, and ate from his food, and drank from his drink, and I saw the seal of prophethood. Hashim said: in the cartilage of his left shoulder, like a gathered fist, in it black moles as if warts."
"21062","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, that he had seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he traveled, said: O Allah, You are the companion in travel and the successor over family. O Allah, accompany us in our travel and succeed us over our family. O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, and the sadness of return, and from decrease after increase, and the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight regarding family and wealth. He said: and Asim was asked about decrease after increase, he said: to turn back after having been (right)."
